@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Typed canvas context requests
+
+Issue: #1698.
+
+HTMLCanvasElement.getContext returns a type determined by the requested context
+name. A broad RenderingContext union cannot safely be discriminated using DOM
+constructor identity across realms. Keep that refusal; express the missing fact
+in the binding instead.
+
+One generic get_context<C: CanvasContext> returns Option<C::Output>. Typed
+canvas_contexts tokens use the existing named unit-struct binding representation;
+dynamic string requests retain the original broad output through the same API.
+The WebIDL generator owns the override and emits the shipped declaration.
+
+Regression tests compile typed and dynamic calls, require direct getContext
+output without instanceof, and execute without DOM constructor globals while
+preserving context object identity and null results. A consumer uses the real
+Canvas 2D API in browser E2E tests.
+
+Rust/JS decision: no observable difference. The browser already guarantees the
+request/result relationship; no cast, approximation or second context registry
+is introduced. Rust checks which operations the returned context supports.
